WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.841
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:48.111 --> 00:55.076
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

3
00:55.785 --> 00:58.079
EPISODE 10

4
00:58.746 --> 01:01.708
His Excellency is here!

5
01:27.609 --> 01:32.113
Today, May 15th, 1932,

6
01:32.739 --> 01:34.699
Joseon's first pneumatic tube system

7
01:34.782 --> 01:37.493
has successfully been unveiled!

8
01:43.625 --> 01:48.004
The Great Japanese Empire's efforts for the development of Joseon

9
01:48.087 --> 01:52.342
have finally borne fruit today.

10
01:53.384 --> 01:54.344
This marks

11
01:55.053 --> 01:59.307
a new milestone in Joseon's modernization

12
01:59.891 --> 02:03.728
and the first step toward Manseon's prosperity…

13
02:04.938 --> 02:06.105
MANSEON MANCHURIA AND JOSEON

14
02:06.189 --> 02:08.274
…eventually reaching Manchukuo!

15
02:32.590 --> 02:34.342
Interpreter Sato!

16
02:35.885 --> 02:37.553
Interpreter Sato, over here.

17
02:47.063 --> 02:49.732
Interpret my speech into English.

18
02:50.692 --> 02:51.693
Yes, sir.

19
03:42.243 --> 03:43.536
Interpreter Sato.

20
03:45.705 --> 03:48.082
Why don't you join us for a toast?

21
03:52.920 --> 03:53.755
Yes, sir.

22
04:08.895 --> 04:10.188
Raise your glasses.

23
04:19.822 --> 04:22.325
It'll go off at 6:20 p.m. Get as far away as you can.

24
04:26.412 --> 04:27.914
Cheers!

25
04:27.997 --> 04:29.207
-Cheers! -Cheers!

26
04:37.131 --> 04:38.091
What's going on?

27
04:44.639 --> 04:45.473
Your Excellency.

28
04:45.556 --> 04:46.391
Yes?

29
04:51.145 --> 04:52.146
What did you say?

30
04:53.189 --> 04:54.232
Excuse me, everyone.

31
05:14.127 --> 05:15.962
Due to an emergency,

32
05:16.045 --> 05:18.339
the banquet has been canceled.

33
05:19.549 --> 05:23.511
We'll update you on the situation once we've sorted things out.

34
05:23.594 --> 05:25.221
Please travel home safely.

35
05:26.180 --> 05:27.265
We're very sorry.

36
05:30.685 --> 05:31.644
Chief of Police.

37
05:34.981 --> 05:37.108
Check security, come to the Governor-General's Office.

38
05:37.775 --> 05:38.609
Yes, sir!

39
05:42.613 --> 05:43.739
Just now,

40
05:43.823 --> 05:46.033
Prime Minister Inukai was attacked in Tokyo.

41
05:46.117 --> 05:48.995
MAY 15TH, 1932, 5:30 P.M. SOLDIERS ATTACKED PRIME MINISTER INUKAI

42
05:52.415 --> 05:53.249
We'd better leave.

43
06:06.596 --> 06:08.055
Please explain to us.

44
06:32.997 --> 06:34.499
-Fourth floor. -Yes, sir.

45
06:50.056 --> 06:51.474
Interpreter Sato!

46
06:53.476 --> 06:56.354
Stop apologizing and explain what's going on.

47
06:56.437 --> 06:57.688
Please return home today.

48
06:58.356 --> 07:00.525
-Interpreter Sato! -Today's banquet is over.

49
07:00.608 --> 07:01.776
Please head home.

50
07:01.859 --> 07:03.152
Excuse me.

51
07:03.736 --> 07:04.612
Mr. Sato!

52
07:07.031 --> 07:07.865
Ms. Keum.

53
07:09.367 --> 07:10.576
Mr. Sato.

54
08:24.567 --> 08:26.736
I'm sorry. Please head home.

55
09:06.484 --> 09:08.527
Are you okay, Ms. Keum?

56
09:09.445 --> 09:10.571
Now, let's get out.

57
09:20.831 --> 09:21.916
Was that a bomb?

58
10:18.848 --> 10:21.434
Someone get a stretcher!

59
10:36.282 --> 10:38.367
Mr. Sato.

60
10:42.079 --> 10:42.997
Mr. Sato!

61
10:45.666 --> 10:47.501
There might be another bomb!

62
10:47.585 --> 10:49.920
Everyone, evacuate immediately!

63
11:00.014 --> 11:01.557
Mr. Sato!

64
11:04.101 --> 11:04.935
Mr. Sato.

65
11:10.941 --> 11:11.776
Ms. Keum.

66
11:13.819 --> 11:15.237
Are you all right?

67
11:15.321 --> 11:17.448
Yes, I'm fine.

68
11:17.531 --> 11:18.532
Are you okay?

69
11:18.616 --> 11:19.617
Yes.

70
11:22.953 --> 11:24.413
You need to get out of here.

71
11:25.164 --> 11:26.081
Someone, please…

72
11:26.999 --> 11:28.167
Somebody,

73
11:28.667 --> 11:30.252
help this person!

74
11:30.961 --> 11:32.046
Get outside, now.

75
11:38.844 --> 11:39.678
Ms. Keum.

76
11:39.762 --> 11:40.846
Mr. Sato!

77
11:41.555 --> 11:42.515
Are you okay?

78
11:51.816 --> 11:54.151
Madam!

79
11:55.110 --> 11:56.070
Madam!

80
11:56.862 --> 11:58.447
What are you doing here? Let's get out.

81
11:58.531 --> 11:59.532
What?

82
12:00.491 --> 12:02.076
We'll all get caught if we don't hurry.

83
12:02.159 --> 12:04.370
You're leaving for America anyway. Why act loyal?

84
12:05.579 --> 12:06.413
Move. Let's go.

85
12:06.497 --> 12:07.623
Myung-nam, hurry.

86
12:07.706 --> 12:10.167
It's okay, Dad. We're almost there.

87
12:24.265 --> 12:25.266
Ms. Keum!

88
12:26.308 --> 12:27.142
Ms. Keum…

89
12:32.147 --> 12:33.190
Ms. Keum!

90
12:47.121 --> 12:48.747
Who's behind all this?

91
12:57.339 --> 12:59.884
Was that explosion your doing too?

92
13:06.891 --> 13:09.935
Tell me. Are you with the Gugukdan too?

93
13:16.609 --> 13:17.443
Independence…

94
13:19.028 --> 13:19.862
for…

95
13:23.657 --> 13:24.742
Korea.

96
13:37.129 --> 13:38.088
Father?

97
13:42.593 --> 13:43.594
He's an independence fighter.

98
13:59.234 --> 14:00.069
Shoot.

99
14:02.071 --> 14:03.113
Kill him.

100
15:17.563 --> 15:18.605
We have to run.

101
15:18.689 --> 15:20.774
The police will be here soon after those gunshots.

102
15:22.526 --> 15:23.861
Inspector General!

103
15:27.948 --> 15:28.866
Inspector General!

104
15:30.826 --> 15:32.202
I just heard the gunshots.

105
15:34.705 --> 15:36.999
A bomb went off in the banquet hall.

106
15:37.082 --> 15:40.210
There may be more bombs. We need to get outside.

107
15:56.894 --> 15:58.312
Songjeon.

108
15:58.854 --> 15:59.980
Songjeon.

109
16:00.731 --> 16:01.899
Songjeon!

110
16:03.650 --> 16:04.485
Songjeon…

111
16:05.360 --> 16:06.570
So-ran.

112
16:18.123 --> 16:19.041
So-ran, we have to go.

113
16:20.250 --> 16:21.418
Songjeon.

114
16:22.169 --> 16:24.296
Wake up, Songjeon!

115
16:26.340 --> 16:27.174
So-ran.

116
17:12.886 --> 17:14.054
Get in, Dad.

117
17:16.849 --> 17:17.724
Hold on.

118
17:21.478 --> 17:23.605
What are you doing? Go to Gyeongseong Station already.

119
17:24.314 --> 17:25.816
What about Mrs. Yoo?

120
17:26.733 --> 17:28.152
Did you not hear me earlier?

121
17:28.235 --> 17:29.194
You should go already.

122
17:29.278 --> 17:30.404
Aren't you going to America?

123
17:30.487 --> 17:31.572
Myung-nam!

124
17:32.072 --> 17:33.198
Get over here!

125
17:33.699 --> 17:36.577
Myung-nam, hurry!

126
17:36.660 --> 17:38.495
Myung-nam, get in here.

127
18:22.956 --> 18:23.790
This way!

128
18:26.877 --> 18:28.420
The suspect went that way!

129
18:28.503 --> 18:29.338
Yes, sir!

130
18:50.567 --> 18:51.485
A woman?

131
18:58.325 --> 18:59.409
How did it go?

132
19:00.035 --> 19:02.287
Did Songjeon make it out?

133
19:04.206 --> 19:05.624
I'm not sure.

134
19:12.339 --> 19:14.216
All the papers for America are in that bag.

135
19:16.009 --> 19:19.012
So-ran packed this for you to eat on the ship.

136
19:23.934 --> 19:27.020
Wipe your face first or you'll get caught at a security check.

137
19:41.827 --> 19:42.786
Hang in there.

138
19:53.088 --> 19:53.922
Mr. Hideo.

139
20:09.813 --> 20:11.148
Let's get going.

140
20:40.969 --> 20:41.845
Shoot.

141
20:44.056 --> 20:44.890
Hideo!

142
21:19.758 --> 21:21.259
I'm done going easy on you.

143
21:22.928 --> 21:23.887
Don't forget.

144
21:24.388 --> 21:27.391
You're nobody if I'm dead.

145
23:19.669 --> 23:26.092
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

146
23:34.643 --> 23:36.937
The Foreign Affairs chief died on the spot.

147
23:37.020 --> 23:38.855
The head of General Affairs at the Communications Bureau

148
23:38.939 --> 23:40.899
died on the way to the hospital.

149
23:42.526 --> 23:43.401
I see.

150
23:44.194 --> 23:47.906
I wonder what you'll have to say for yourself this time, Inspector General,

151
23:48.698 --> 23:50.617
with that big mouth of yours.

152
23:50.700 --> 23:53.620
Didn't you preach about using the situation to our advantage?

153
23:55.664 --> 24:00.252
You swore you'd round up every last one of those subversives.

154
24:01.127 --> 24:03.046
A bomb, here in the Government-General?

155
24:04.839 --> 24:06.049
How dare you

156
24:06.132 --> 24:09.386
make a fool of me!

157
24:11.012 --> 24:12.389
I take full responsibility.

158
24:12.472 --> 24:13.557
I'm sorry.

159
24:13.640 --> 24:14.933
You incompetent fool!

160
24:16.142 --> 24:19.062
A colonial resident like you never deserved the position in the first place.

161
24:19.145 --> 24:20.564
Step down now!

162
24:24.192 --> 24:26.111
Will that solve everything?

163
24:27.654 --> 24:28.613
What?

164
24:32.117 --> 24:33.743
If I step down,

165
24:34.953 --> 24:37.914
will everyone forget the bomb went off at the Government-General?

166
24:37.998 --> 24:39.040
Inspector General!

167
24:39.124 --> 24:42.252
Yun Bong-gil's bombing in Shanghai was only two weeks ago.

168
24:43.128 --> 24:45.964
The League of Nations team arrives in Joseon in under two months.

169
24:46.047 --> 24:47.090
At a time like this,

170
24:47.841 --> 24:50.969
a bomb goes off at the Government-General of Joseon

171
24:51.052 --> 24:52.762
and the inspector general resigns…

172
24:53.972 --> 24:56.516
What will the international community make of that?

173
24:57.475 --> 25:01.354
The whole thing happened in front of the foreign press.

174
25:01.438 --> 25:03.648
How are you supposed to bury that?

175
25:03.732 --> 25:04.774
Today's incident

176
25:05.984 --> 25:09.362
was a random act by a Japanese man who's mentally unstable.

177
25:10.488 --> 25:14.534
No independence fighters ever infiltrated the Government-General.

178
25:15.201 --> 25:16.286
This is a time

179
25:17.162 --> 25:19.456
when Joseon must appear peaceful.

180
25:21.207 --> 25:22.083
Your Excellency.

181
25:24.711 --> 25:26.630
It went just as we planned.

182
25:28.048 --> 25:29.674
The outrage fades quickly.

183
25:29.758 --> 25:32.385
It's cleaning up the mess that matters.

184
25:33.637 --> 25:36.056
When someone offers to wield the sword for us,

185
25:36.139 --> 25:37.807
there's no reason to say no.

186
25:40.143 --> 25:40.977
Yes, sir.

187
25:41.061 --> 25:43.938
I'll make sure we catch the culprit tonight.

188
26:14.427 --> 26:15.845
I'm sorry.

189
26:16.388 --> 26:17.472
I'm sorry.

190
26:18.348 --> 26:19.724
This pawn ticket.

191
26:20.350 --> 26:22.018
Why'd you put it here?

192
26:22.977 --> 26:24.312
Do you not want

193
26:24.396 --> 26:26.856
anything to do with someone like me anymore?

194
27:29.127 --> 27:30.044
Ga-kyung.

195
27:30.712 --> 27:34.174
When you get to America, live life your way.

196
27:35.717 --> 27:38.386
Neither I nor my daughter could do that.

197
27:39.012 --> 27:42.182
But I want you to have that chance, no matter what.

198
27:43.892 --> 27:45.268
Be happy.

199
27:46.478 --> 27:47.687
You have to.

200
27:54.819 --> 27:57.864
CASTELLA

201
28:01.367 --> 28:02.994
Just as he was leaving,

202
28:03.703 --> 28:05.121
he said to me…

203
28:06.581 --> 28:07.707
"When spring comes,

204
28:09.292 --> 28:11.252
let's take Seo-hee to Gyeongseong

205
28:12.212 --> 28:14.047
and have some castella."

206
28:19.677 --> 28:20.678
Incheon!

207
28:20.762 --> 28:24.349
The train for Incheon is about to depart.

208
28:58.424 --> 28:59.259
Watch your step.

209
29:03.388 --> 29:05.598
I'm not sure it was a good idea to come home.

210
29:06.224 --> 29:08.184
You should get more treatment and rest.

211
29:08.268 --> 29:10.478
They'll get suspicious if our house is empty.

212
29:11.563 --> 29:12.605
I can manage.

213
29:13.565 --> 29:14.399
All right.

214
29:16.025 --> 29:17.694
But don't push yourself too hard.

215
29:30.039 --> 29:31.332
Who is it?

216
29:31.916 --> 29:33.668
We're from the Government-General.

217
29:44.929 --> 29:46.347
What's going on?

218
29:54.105 --> 29:55.106
Mr. Hideo.

219
30:10.788 --> 30:11.623
So-ran.

220
30:12.206 --> 30:15.001
The Government-General sent the police with Mr. Hideo.

221
30:26.846 --> 30:28.014
Mr. Hideo.

222
30:28.097 --> 30:29.098
Hello.

223
30:29.891 --> 30:31.309
Sorry to bother you so late.

224
30:32.018 --> 30:33.186
We're checking everyone

225
30:33.269 --> 30:35.772
who may have been hurt at the banquet today.

226
30:35.855 --> 30:38.524
Did you… not get hurt?

227
30:40.818 --> 30:42.320
Honey, what's all this about?

228
30:44.113 --> 30:44.989
Mr. Hideo.

229
30:45.073 --> 30:47.617
I appreciate you checking on us, but it's awfully late--

230
30:47.700 --> 30:48.701
Wait.

231
30:49.702 --> 30:51.454
You're missing one earring.

232
30:52.288 --> 30:53.456
A pearl earring, at that.

233
30:58.795 --> 30:59.963
Put those guns away.

234
31:03.299 --> 31:04.509
Have you lost your mind?

235
31:04.592 --> 31:06.052
Stay back.

236
31:10.181 --> 31:11.349
I put the other earring

237
31:12.308 --> 31:14.227
in here.

238
31:14.310 --> 31:15.687
Stand back.

239
31:19.232 --> 31:20.566
I'll check.

240
31:27.365 --> 31:28.199
No.

241
31:30.952 --> 31:32.412
I'll check it.

242
31:34.622 --> 31:35.832
Put the guns down and step back.

243
32:01.566 --> 32:02.400
Madam!

244
32:03.651 --> 32:04.777
I'm back.

245
32:06.863 --> 32:07.947
Are you upstairs?

246
32:13.745 --> 32:15.329
I'm back!

247
32:15.413 --> 32:17.165
-Madam! -Freeze!

248
32:29.510 --> 32:30.928
Mr. Sato.

249
32:31.637 --> 32:34.682
Are you here to arrest us?

250
32:35.725 --> 32:37.143
Put the guns down.

251
32:38.895 --> 32:39.729
Put them down.

252
32:43.983 --> 32:45.568
I'm Keum Seo-hee, an English interpreter trainee

253
32:45.651 --> 32:48.362
at the Government-General, and I live here with them.

254
32:49.197 --> 32:54.952
I work with Interpreter Sato Hideo here at the Government-General.

255
32:59.749 --> 33:01.000
Are you okay, Madam?

256
33:02.543 --> 33:03.628
You look shaken up--

257
33:03.711 --> 33:04.879
Back off!

258
33:07.381 --> 33:08.216
Okay.

259
33:08.299 --> 33:09.258
Mr. Sato.

260
33:09.342 --> 33:12.136
Please check the drawer for the other earring.

261
33:25.775 --> 33:26.651
Mr. Sato.

262
33:27.485 --> 33:28.861
Under your foot…

263
33:40.873 --> 33:41.833
Oh my.

264
33:41.916 --> 33:44.085
Why does this keep falling out?

265
33:44.168 --> 33:46.337
It almost got crushed under your foot.

266
33:47.547 --> 33:49.882
I'll go get this fixed tomorrow.

267
33:55.555 --> 33:57.140
Is that all you needed?

268
33:59.475 --> 34:02.603
You said you were checking on people who may have been hurt from the bombing.

269
34:03.187 --> 34:05.106
Why are you pointing guns at us?

270
34:05.731 --> 34:07.817
The bombing at the Government-General?

271
34:09.318 --> 34:13.531
Wait, are you here to find the bomber?

272
34:14.198 --> 34:15.575
We can't comment on that.

273
34:15.658 --> 34:18.327
We need to check for shoulder injury.

274
34:18.411 --> 34:21.164
Both ladies who attended today's banquet.

275
34:21.247 --> 34:23.291
Please pull down your tops and show your shoulders.

276
34:29.297 --> 34:31.966
How dare you make such a demand of my wife?

277
34:32.049 --> 34:33.176
Step back, please.

278
34:38.431 --> 34:39.265
Shoulders?

279
34:40.183 --> 34:41.809
Just a moment.

280
34:44.395 --> 34:45.229
Like this?

281
34:46.647 --> 34:47.690
Will this do?

282
34:50.735 --> 34:52.278
I'm clear, right?

283
34:55.781 --> 34:57.408
Yes, you're clear.

284
34:59.452 --> 35:03.289
Now let me check the madam.

285
35:03.372 --> 35:04.207
That's enough.

286
35:11.047 --> 35:12.048
Let's get going.

287
35:12.131 --> 35:13.090
No, sir.

288
35:13.633 --> 35:14.800
We still need to check.

289
35:16.344 --> 35:17.553
Sorry about the trouble.

290
35:27.396 --> 35:28.231
-Excuse us. -Excuse us.

291
35:52.421 --> 35:53.756
Sorry to have caused you trouble.

292
35:54.340 --> 35:55.299
We'll be in touch.

293
35:55.967 --> 35:56.801
Okay.

294
36:23.953 --> 36:25.371
They're gone.

295
36:27.415 --> 36:29.125
Madam! Are you okay?

296
36:30.084 --> 36:30.918
You're bleeding.

297
36:31.794 --> 36:33.129
Why are you back?

298
36:33.212 --> 36:34.046
What?

299
36:34.130 --> 36:36.841
You were supposed to be on the train. Why'd you come back?

300
36:36.924 --> 36:39.260
That's not important right now. Wait--

301
36:39.343 --> 36:41.220
Going to America was your dream.

302
36:41.304 --> 36:42.888
So why would you come back?

303
36:47.101 --> 36:48.769
I can't stand owing anyone anything.

304
36:49.603 --> 36:50.438
What?

305
36:50.521 --> 36:52.982
You gave me this thick envelope, so I opened it.

306
36:53.524 --> 36:56.027
It was the three months' pay you'd originally promised me.

307
36:57.028 --> 36:58.988
I said I'd quit after just one month.

308
36:59.071 --> 37:00.573
There's no taking it back, okay?

309
37:00.656 --> 37:02.491
I can't give back what you've already paid me.

310
37:03.659 --> 37:06.162
So I'll finish the full three months.

311
37:07.455 --> 37:08.706
Send me to America after that.

312
37:10.082 --> 37:13.002
If I took the money and bailed, I'd be a crook,

313
37:13.794 --> 37:15.338
not a spy.

314
37:18.466 --> 37:19.300
So-ran.

315
37:28.184 --> 37:29.393
How did you find out?

316
37:33.230 --> 37:34.190
The thing is…

317
37:54.960 --> 37:56.545
We'd like your cooperation.

318
38:21.112 --> 38:23.072
Why are you headed to Incheon?

319
38:26.784 --> 38:29.328
I'm going to meet an American missionary.

320
38:29.412 --> 38:31.372
I've agreed to look after their baby.

321
38:43.300 --> 38:44.176
Raise your arms like this.

322
38:49.432 --> 38:50.266
Do this with your arms.

323
38:57.940 --> 38:59.275
I don't think she's been hurt.

324
39:03.404 --> 39:04.947
Over there, pearl earrings…

325
39:07.032 --> 39:08.659
See if she has both earrings.

326
39:08.742 --> 39:09.577
Yes, sir.

327
39:12.746 --> 39:13.873
Pearl earrings?

328
39:16.876 --> 39:17.710
She has both.

329
39:26.385 --> 39:27.428
Thank you.

330
39:31.640 --> 39:33.601
We appreciate your cooperation.

331
40:06.175 --> 40:08.010
Well, that's what happened.

332
40:13.474 --> 40:14.308
I see.

333
40:18.103 --> 40:19.730
So where'd you get the earring?

334
40:20.773 --> 40:21.649
The earring?

335
40:21.732 --> 40:25.736
THE FIRST JONGNO PAWNSHOP

336
40:27.279 --> 40:28.113
Mister!

337
40:28.197 --> 40:30.658
Mister, open the door!

338
40:30.741 --> 40:31.992
Wake up!

339
40:32.076 --> 40:33.202
Mister!

340
40:33.827 --> 40:35.704
-Mister. -Who is it?

341
40:35.788 --> 40:38.457
-It's me, Ga-kyung. -Who is it?

342
40:38.541 --> 40:39.959
Mister!

343
40:40.042 --> 40:41.210
Hurry up and open the door.

344
40:41.293 --> 40:43.087
Don't you know what time it is?

345
40:43.170 --> 40:44.004
Come on!

346
40:44.088 --> 40:47.758
Apparently, it's all the rage among stylish ladies these days.

347
40:48.384 --> 40:52.680
I hear lots of men buy them as gifts for their girlfriends.

348
40:58.644 --> 41:00.354
I promised to give it back to the pawnshop tomorrow.

349
41:02.898 --> 41:06.569
I never expected Sato Hideo to show up with the police.

350
41:06.652 --> 41:08.821
He's clearly suspicious of us.

351
41:09.780 --> 41:10.614
Even so,

352
41:11.532 --> 41:14.868
do you really think he came because he suspects us?

353
41:16.537 --> 41:21.542
The police tried to check her shoulder, but he stopped them, so they just left.

354
41:22.751 --> 41:24.712
He probably only realized later how serious it was

355
41:24.795 --> 41:28.382
to barge into a foreign reporter's house and try to make a woman undress

356
41:28.924 --> 41:30.217
in times like these.

357
41:36.640 --> 41:38.309
Songjeon has been killed.

358
41:41.604 --> 41:42.438
What?

359
41:45.024 --> 41:46.066
You mean…

360
41:47.026 --> 41:50.446
the one who went in as a cook?

361
41:51.071 --> 41:52.197
Yes.

362
41:54.283 --> 41:55.826
Sato Hideo killed him.

363
41:59.038 --> 42:00.372
I saw it myself.

364
42:01.957 --> 42:03.083
Sato Hideo

365
42:04.001 --> 42:06.003
murdered Songjeon.

366
42:20.392 --> 42:21.352
Oh no, Hideo.

367
42:22.311 --> 42:23.604
What happened?

368
42:24.146 --> 42:25.856
-We need to call a doctor. -No.

369
42:26.482 --> 42:27.483
There's no need.

370
42:29.568 --> 42:30.444
Goodnight.

371
43:01.475 --> 43:04.561
The accomplice fled with a gunshot wound to the shoulder.

372
43:05.187 --> 43:08.482
Go to every female guest's house and check for gunshot wounds.

373
43:08.565 --> 43:09.483
-Yes, sir! -Yes, sir!

374
43:09.566 --> 43:13.821
The suspect left one pearl earring at the scene. Use it as a lead!

375
43:14.530 --> 43:15.531
-Yes, sir! -Yes, sir!

376
43:20.703 --> 43:23.664
She's the wife of Yoo Philip, an American correspondent from WWP News.

377
43:34.383 --> 43:35.259
Mr. Hideo.

378
43:44.268 --> 43:45.227
Hold on!

379
43:58.365 --> 44:00.701
Mr. Yoo is an important foreign correspondent.

380
44:00.784 --> 44:02.828
Conduct the investigation carefully.

381
44:02.911 --> 44:03.954
If handled poorly,

382
44:04.037 --> 44:06.582
this could become a diplomatic issue. That's why I came along.

383
44:06.665 --> 44:07.875
-Yes, sir. -Yes, sir.

384
44:10.502 --> 44:11.462
This way.

385
44:18.218 --> 44:19.261
Mr. Sato.

386
44:20.053 --> 44:21.388
Under your foot…

387
44:24.850 --> 44:25.726
Like this?

388
44:39.239 --> 44:40.532
It can't be…

389
46:06.618 --> 46:08.412
On the night of May 15th,

390
46:08.495 --> 46:10.747
the Gugukdan carried out a bomb attack

391
46:10.831 --> 46:14.042
at a pneumatic tube opening banquet at the Government-General,

392
46:14.751 --> 46:17.462
resulting in heavy casualties among Japanese officials.

393
46:21.049 --> 46:24.887
Comrade Songjeon, a Japanese member of the Gugukdan who died in the attack,

394
46:24.970 --> 46:26.513
will not have sacrificed his life in vain.

395
46:27.472 --> 46:29.892
We will remember our fallen comrade, Songjeon,

396
46:31.268 --> 46:34.396
and never stop fighting for Joseon's independence.

397
46:34.897 --> 46:35.731
Joseon…

398
46:36.940 --> 46:38.942
will achieve independence, without fail.

399
46:49.411 --> 46:51.496
Extra!

400
46:53.665 --> 46:56.043
Extra!

401
47:20.776 --> 47:23.654
GUGUKDAN CARRIES OUT BOMBING AT GOVERNMENT-GENERAL

402
47:23.737 --> 47:24.905
It's in the paper.

403
47:25.948 --> 47:27.032
That's a relief.

404
47:28.325 --> 47:30.160
Did Suzuki tip them off?

405
47:31.912 --> 47:32.996
Myung-nam.

406
47:33.497 --> 47:35.499
Myung-nam, did you see this?

407
47:36.083 --> 47:36.959
What is it?

408
47:37.668 --> 47:40.379
Those lunatics. Have they completely lost their minds?

409
47:40.462 --> 47:42.339
GOVERNMENT-GENERAL BOMBING BY A DERANGED LONER

410
47:42.422 --> 47:44.508
How dare they cause a ruckus in that hallowed place?

411
47:44.591 --> 47:46.093
They're utterly shameless.

412
47:46.635 --> 47:49.471
At least the culprit took his own life.

413
47:49.554 --> 47:50.722
It's a relief.

414
47:51.932 --> 47:53.100
Lunatics?

415
47:55.268 --> 47:56.269
Haven't you seen this?

416
47:57.270 --> 47:59.022
The Gugukdan was behind yesterday's attack.

417
47:59.106 --> 48:00.857
The culprit wasn't crazy or suicidal--

418
48:00.941 --> 48:01.984
Enough!

419
48:02.067 --> 48:03.443
The Gugukdan?

420
48:05.195 --> 48:07.614
Don't even utter that disgraceful name.

421
48:08.198 --> 48:11.034
And don't read seditious newspapers like this.

422
48:13.870 --> 48:16.707
Anyway, you know what, Myung-nam?

423
48:17.708 --> 48:20.502
Heaven was on my side.

424
48:22.963 --> 48:25.632
I had a stomachache, so I was in the bathroom.

425
48:25.716 --> 48:28.927
I was upset about missing the toast at the banquet.

426
48:29.511 --> 48:33.056
But thanks to that, I got away from the bombing without a scratch.

427
48:33.140 --> 48:36.476
I'm telling you, Heaven is looking out for me.

428
48:38.437 --> 48:39.730
I can't believe it.

429
48:41.148 --> 48:42.315
Have some coffee, Dad.

430
48:42.941 --> 48:44.192
All right.

431
48:47.738 --> 48:49.031
Oh my goodness.

432
48:49.114 --> 48:51.491
The coffee tastes extra sweet today.

433
48:51.575 --> 48:55.120
Nothing beats the coffee my daughter makes.

434
48:59.082 --> 49:01.501
Sir, these documents need your signature.

435
49:06.256 --> 49:07.966
Ouch, my stomach.

436
49:08.759 --> 49:09.801
Hang on.

437
49:21.271 --> 49:22.397
The medicine in his drink

438
49:23.315 --> 49:25.650
at the banquet yesterday must've been strong.

439
49:25.734 --> 49:26.610
No.

440
49:27.944 --> 49:30.322
He was saying things I didn't want to hear this morning,

441
49:30.405 --> 49:31.573
so I put the rest in his coffee.

442
49:36.411 --> 49:37.245
Young-bok.

443
49:38.872 --> 49:42.125
If Kim Seung-eok, Joseon's most notorious traitor, weren't my dad,

444
49:42.876 --> 49:46.213
would our comrades have suggested using laxatives to protect him?

445
49:47.297 --> 49:48.131
Miss.

446
49:49.883 --> 49:51.134
I don't know anymore

447
49:52.094 --> 49:53.386
if I did the right thing.

448
49:55.680 --> 49:59.059
We're fighting to get rid of pro-Japanese traitors for independence.

449
50:00.143 --> 50:02.354
So was it right to save my own father?

450
50:06.024 --> 50:08.443
How can he be so shameless?

451
50:09.486 --> 50:13.365
Songjeon is being humiliated like this.

452
50:30.632 --> 50:31.842
Pardon me.

453
50:59.494 --> 51:00.412
Sir,

454
51:01.997 --> 51:04.207
it seems the Gugukdan carried out yesterday's attack.

455
51:04.291 --> 51:05.292
I saw it already.

456
51:06.668 --> 51:09.921
This morning, the governor-general called me to his residence and yelled at me.

457
51:12.299 --> 51:13.341
I'm sorry.

458
51:13.425 --> 51:15.719
Joseon Central News says

459
51:15.802 --> 51:19.264
they published the story based on an anonymous tip.

460
51:19.806 --> 51:21.349
But they claim they burned the original.

461
51:22.309 --> 51:23.768
I ordered the paper to be shut down.

462
51:23.852 --> 51:26.271
And none of the women had gunshot wounds?

463
51:29.608 --> 51:31.318
There were at least four women

464
51:32.110 --> 51:34.321
at the banquet

465
51:35.405 --> 51:37.073
wearing pearl earrings yesterday.

466
51:40.869 --> 51:44.623
And none of these four had gunshot wounds or any other injuries?

467
51:44.706 --> 51:45.957
About that…

468
51:48.084 --> 51:50.795
There's one thing you need to confirm.

469
51:51.421 --> 51:52.255
What is it?

470
51:52.339 --> 51:54.591
It'd be better to hear from them directly.

471
51:55.717 --> 51:56.551
Come in!

472
52:04.476 --> 52:06.895
These officers went to Yoo Philip's house last night.

473
52:10.065 --> 52:11.191
Who is it?

474
52:11.274 --> 52:13.193
We're from the Government-General.

475
52:15.528 --> 52:17.447
We went with Interpreter Sato.

476
52:18.365 --> 52:19.199
With Hideo?

477
52:19.282 --> 52:20.450
Correct, sir.

478
52:20.533 --> 52:23.203
Did you check the woman for gunshot wounds?

479
52:23.286 --> 52:26.831
We checked a young woman named Keum Seo-hee, and she was clear.

480
52:27.791 --> 52:29.542
But the American reporter's wife…

481
52:29.626 --> 52:30.877
we didn't check her.

482
52:30.961 --> 52:32.545
You didn't check her?

483
52:32.629 --> 52:34.631
That's right. The thing is…

484
52:35.298 --> 52:36.132
Let's get going.

485
52:36.216 --> 52:40.345
Interpreter Sato said we didn't need to check her.

486
52:45.809 --> 52:47.310
All right. You may leave.

487
52:47.394 --> 52:48.395
-Yes, sir! -Yes, sir!

488
52:53.525 --> 52:54.484
What should we do?

489
53:06.538 --> 53:09.666
Allow me to introduce my wife. She's Chinese.

490
53:11.668 --> 53:12.919
What's going on?

491
53:14.713 --> 53:17.257
Mrs. Yoo's button came off.

492
53:23.346 --> 53:25.724
Find out whether anyone in Kyeam-ri

493
53:26.516 --> 53:27.684
knows this woman.

494
53:32.856 --> 53:35.859
Do you think she's Keum Seok-jung's wife?

495
53:49.414 --> 53:52.250
Since the Gugukdan was behind yesterday's attack,

496
53:53.501 --> 53:55.670
could she be one of them too?

497
54:02.427 --> 54:03.261
Good morning.

498
54:06.973 --> 54:07.807
Who is it?

499
54:08.683 --> 54:09.851
It's Interpreter Sato.

500
54:16.232 --> 54:17.275
Oh, Hideo!

501
54:17.984 --> 54:18.902
Hello.

502
54:21.780 --> 54:22.614
Please come in.

503
54:23.198 --> 54:24.032
By the way,

504
54:24.115 --> 54:25.909
I heard about your engagement.

505
54:26.409 --> 54:27.410
Congratulations.

506
54:27.494 --> 54:28.828
Thanks.

507
54:46.262 --> 54:47.597
Soon you won't walk around

508
54:47.680 --> 54:51.351
with your head held high, pretending to be Japanese.

509
54:53.311 --> 54:54.562
Josenjing.

510
55:03.238 --> 55:04.572
Your wound is pretty deep.

511
55:05.573 --> 55:07.367
Shouldn't you get it checked at the hospital?

512
55:07.450 --> 55:08.368
Don't worry.

513
55:08.451 --> 55:11.621
There's no shortage of people who want me dead.

514
55:12.997 --> 55:13.832
But…

515
55:15.166 --> 55:16.251
I'm not going to die.

516
55:46.614 --> 55:48.032
I acted rashly yesterday.

517
55:48.658 --> 55:52.036
I shouldn't have let my feelings get the better of me. Forgive me.

518
55:52.120 --> 55:55.373
Should I be glad you've finally realized it?

519
55:56.916 --> 55:57.750
I'm sorry.

520
56:03.882 --> 56:04.716
Apart from…

521
56:06.551 --> 56:08.511
finding out that the Gugukdan did it,

522
56:09.095 --> 56:10.597
did you find anything else?

523
56:18.146 --> 56:19.355
Why do you want to know?

524
56:19.439 --> 56:21.399
I'm worried about you, Father.

525
56:22.484 --> 56:23.776
Yesterday's attack was serious.

526
56:27.113 --> 56:30.783
Focus on the foreign press and prepare for the League of Nations' visit.

527
56:32.368 --> 56:34.037
That's what you need to worry about,

528
56:35.205 --> 56:36.915
nothing else, Interpreter Sato.

529
56:39.209 --> 56:40.460
Yes, understood.

530
56:40.543 --> 56:44.088
The governor-general will be working from his residence for the time being.

531
56:46.508 --> 56:47.342
Keep that in mind.

532
56:48.676 --> 56:49.928
Understood.

533
56:56.601 --> 56:59.020
Why did you go to Yoo Philip's house last night?

534
57:10.990 --> 57:12.825
Given how important the foreign press is,

535
57:12.909 --> 57:15.537
I was worried the officers might offend them, so I went along.

536
57:18.081 --> 57:20.083
Only Yoo Philip's story was in line

537
57:20.166 --> 57:22.418
with the official position of the Government-General.

538
57:24.462 --> 57:25.338
He reported

539
57:26.005 --> 57:28.383
that a mentally unstable Japanese man was behind the attack.

540
57:29.676 --> 57:31.636
You seem to be getting along well with him.

541
57:32.762 --> 57:33.680
Fine. You may go.

542
57:34.806 --> 57:35.640
Yes, sir.

543
57:55.535 --> 57:58.871
ENGLISH TRANSLATION UNIT

544
58:04.335 --> 58:06.004
I saw it myself.

545
58:06.588 --> 58:07.714
Sato Hideo

546
58:08.631 --> 58:10.675
murdered Songjeon.

547
58:25.648 --> 58:27.108
Hello.

548
58:42.707 --> 58:43.541
Ms. Keum.

549
58:45.835 --> 58:46.669
Yes?

550
58:56.471 --> 58:57.305
What am I…

551
59:01.351 --> 59:03.269
supposed to call you?

552
59:05.229 --> 59:06.064
Sorry?

553
59:06.147 --> 59:07.357
Keum Seo-hee?

554
59:09.484 --> 59:10.401
Lee Gae-ttong?

555
59:12.236 --> 59:14.656
I'm not sure what you mean out of the blue.

556
59:17.241 --> 59:18.117
So…

557
59:23.831 --> 59:25.500
what's your real name?

558
59:36.177 --> 59:37.011
You are…

559
59:39.889 --> 59:40.973
a spy, aren't you?

560
01:00:36.779 --> 01:00:40.700
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

561
01:00:43.244 --> 01:00:44.120
Her cover's been blown?

562
01:00:44.579 --> 01:00:47.206
Isn't there a Josenjing who comes and goes at the Government-General

563
01:00:47.290 --> 01:00:49.417
every day, riding on an American's coattails?

564
01:00:49.500 --> 01:00:50.793
A pawn ticket?

565
01:00:50.877 --> 01:00:52.420
Looks like I'm an unwelcome guest.

566
01:00:53.004 --> 01:00:54.630
But since I'm already here,

567
01:00:54.714 --> 01:00:55.882
you may as well keep acting.

568
01:00:55.965 --> 01:00:59.135
Then wouldn't it be better to get rid of her?

569
01:01:00.303 --> 01:01:01.345
Who are you people?

570
01:01:03.514 --> 01:01:05.099
Do you believe people can change?

571
01:01:05.183 --> 01:01:07.643
I think they can.

572
01:01:07.727 --> 01:01:08.936
Nice to meet you,

573
01:01:10.021 --> 01:01:11.063
Ms. Lee Ga-kyung.

574
01:01:17.779 --> 01:01:20.114
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
